- How would you adapt for tenant churn or abrupt CKNE shifts?
- What metrics would you expose to observe fairness and SLA adherence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant degradation control in real-time multi-hop pipelines under load.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health propagation across hops
- Per-tenant circuit-breakers and edge state
- Minute-by-minute control loops with queue depth and SLA awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example control logic sketch (pseudo)
type TenantState = { id:string; ckne:string; queue:number; sla:'high'|'medium'|'low'; mode:'OPEN'|'HALF'|'CLOSED' };
function tick(states:TenantState[]) {
  for (const s of states){
    const th = s.sla==='high'? 100: s.sla==='medium'? 60: 40;
    if (s.ckne === 'red' || s.queue > th) s.mode = 'OPEN';
    else if (s.ckne === 'yellow') s.mode = 'HALF';
    else s.mode = 'CLOSED';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Probes a practical intersection of CKNE health monitoring, observability, and production safety. It tests the ability to trade trace fidelity for overhead under real bursts in a multi-tenant mesh.

## Key Concepts
- Adaptive sampling based on CKNE health signals
- Per-service and per-tenant quotas with sticky sampling
- Overhead vs fidelity trade-offs in high-load scenarios
- Concrete measurement plan and burst testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldSample(ctx, health) {
  // health: { tailLatMs, errorRate, cpu, io }
  const base = 0.25;
  const penalty = health.tailLatMs > 200 ? 0.15 : 0;
  const errorPenalty = health.errorRate > 0.02 ? 0.1 : 0;
  const quotaBoost = health.cpu > 0.8 ? -0.05 : 0;
  const rate = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, base - penalty - errorPenalty + quotaBoost));
  return Math.random() < rate;
}
```

